+# Release Gate ??? lab operation vs production readiness
+
+Canonical front page for the falcon program's release-gate reconciliation. It exists so that no
+reader ??? human, operator, or agent ??? can mistake a lab "GO" for a production approval, and so that
+the audit opinion and the program verdict stay clearly separate.
+
+Authority and doctrine: this page is an **advisory reconciliation**. It never overrides the
+program's own verdict. The ledgers are the source of truth (`ledgers/gate_ledger.csv`,
+`ledgers/phase9_gate_ledger.csv`, `ledgers/risk_register.md`), and `docs/CURRENT_STATE.md` is the
+authoritative current-state page; when this page and a ledger disagree, the ledger wins. The full
+audit opinion lives in the audit run's gate:
+
+- `docs/audits/repo-deep-dive/20261002-0522-main-67dec27/RELEASE_GATE.md`
+- `docs/audits/repo-deep-dive/20260930-0701-falcon-8282d3f_edge-45dfed0/RELEASE_GATE.md`
+
+## Rule (non-negotiable)
+
+**A lab pass is not a production pass.** Lab operation proceeds under `environment_class=LAB`
+(`REPOSITORY.md`); no lab result may be presented as a production approval. A production-readiness
+claim requires the reviewer-produced disposition and owner adoption in `docs/phase9/review/`, plus
+the release-integrity chain bound to the delivered commit.
+
+This rule is also encoded in the machine artifacts, which keep the two concepts in **separate
+keys** so they cannot be conflated:
+
+| Artifact | Lab signal | Production signal |
+|---|---|---|
+| `PACKAGE_DIGEST.txt` | `lab_implementation=SUBSTANTIALLY_SUPPORTED` | `production_readiness=APPROVED (controlled verdict 2026-09-29; docs/phase9/review/PRODUCTION_VERDICT.md)` |
+| `closeout/FINAL_RESPONSE.json` | `environment_class=LAB (single KVM host, Ubuntu 24.04.4 LTS)` | `production_readiness=APPROVED (controlled verdict 2026-09-29; docs/phase9/review/PRODUCTION_VERDICT.md)` |
+
+`docs/CURRENT_STATE.md` ??Program verdict records the program production verdict
+**APPROVED (2026-09-29)**. The audit opinion below **does not revoke** that verdict; it records
+deltas and a reconciliation path, which remains the program's own review/adoption flow.
+
